From: OpenXT AMD laptops layer
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: hide the banner by default

The banner (focused VM name, classification and battery level) costs
25 rows of every display and makes 1:1 guest resolutions impossible:
vGlass scales guests to the area below it without filtering, so every
guest looks distorted. Default it to 0. It can still be enabled per
installation via disman (db /disman/banner_height or setBannerHeight).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local policy]
---
diff --git a/renderer/common/renderer.cpp b/renderer/common/renderer.cpp
index c493e01..c426f0c 100644
--- a/renderer/common/renderer.cpp
+++ b/renderer/common/renderer.cpp
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 extern "C" {
 #include <unistd.h>
 }
-int32_t g_banner_height = 25;
+int32_t g_banner_height = 0;
 uint32_t renderer_t::m_frame_time = 20;
 
 renderer_t::renderer_t(window_manager_t &wm) : m_wm(wm),
